<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       FURNACEBEAST_THERMAL_CYCLE_1, part 3/4 — how the furnace-beast gets to
       decide.

       Same supported modder hook the fire-hawk uses and for the same reasons:
       Core's Defs/ThinkTreeDefs/Animal.xml carries
       <li Class="ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag"><insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag></li>,
       and a ThinkTreeDef declaring that insertTag is spliced in there. Not a
       Harmony transpiler, not a PatchOperation into the vanilla Animal tree.
       No MayRequire: Animal_PreWander is Core.

       NO FACTION GATE, matching the fire-hawk. A tamed furnace-beast walks into
       your burn and strips your thornvine exactly as a wild one does — the
       ruling that a kept beast "never stops being a fire hazard" is the same
       ruling, and a ThinkNode_ConditionalHasFaction wrapper here would quietly
       undo it.

       The species gate is the comp (CompFurnaceThermalCharge), checked in C# by
       the job-giver: there is no per-species XML hook at this splice point.

       insertPriority 54: just under the fire-hawk's 55, so the two igniters do
       not contend for a number, and above RimProperty's theft nodes (50).
  ======================================================================== -->
  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RM_FurnaceBeast_ThermalCycle</defName>
    <insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag>
    <insertPriority>54</insertPriority>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Tagger">
      <tagToGive>Misc</tagToGive>
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.JobGiver_RUT_FurnaceThermalCycle" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
